{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  note: x taken as real on [-3, 3] (say \"integer x\" for whole numbers)\n  ucas: it(x: real in -3..3) = x^4 - 4*x^2 + 3\n  ucas: crit it\ncritical points of it:\n  it' = 4x^3 - 8x\n  x ≈ -1.414213562: local minimum, it = -1\n  x ≈ 0: local maximum, it = 3\n  x ≈ 1.414213562: local minimum, it = -1\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "what are the critical points of x^4 - 4x^2 + 3 from -3 to 3?", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": ["it(x: real in -3..3) = x^4 - 4*x^2 + 3", "crit it"], "understood": true, "results": [{"kind": "crit", "derivative": "4x^3 - 8x", "points": [{"x": -1.414213562373095, "kind": "local minimum", "value": -0.9999999999999996}, {"x": 0, "kind": "local maximum", "value": 3}, {"x": 1.414213562373095, "kind": "local minimum", "value": -0.9999999999999996}]}]}, "notes": [{"kind": "rule", "text": "x taken as real on [-3, 3] (say \"integer x\" for whole numbers)"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "proof": {"kind": "numeric", "text": "sign changes of the derivative on a grid, refined by bisection"}, "files": [], "text": "  note: x taken as real on [-3, 3] (say \"integer x\" for whole numbers)\n  ucas: it(x: real in -3..3) = x^4 - 4*x^2 + 3\n  ucas: crit it\ncritical points of it:\n  it' = 4x^3 - 8x\n  x ≈ -1.414213562: local minimum, it = -1\n  x ≈ 0: local maximum, it = 3\n  x ≈ 1.414213562: local minimum, it = -1\n"}, "isError": false}}
